WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Learning becomes durable when you actively retrieve an idea instead of only rereading it.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Spacing those retrieval attempts over time makes the memory easier to access later.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Connect each new concept to an example you already understand.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Then explain the concept in your own words and notice where the explanation breaks down.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Those gaps tell you exactly what to revisit next.
